      "kind": "teaching_action_meta",
      "conceptId": "math.prob.generating-function",
      "title": "PARTIAL (MC-3: PGFs add instead of multiply) → \"For INDEPENDENT X,Y: G_{X+Y}(z)=E[z^{X+Y}]=E[z^X·z^Y]=E[z^X]E[z^Y]=G_X(z)G_Y(z). They MULTIPLY. Intuition: the PGF of a sum is the PRODUCT of PGFs (like Laplace transforms of convolutions). PMF convolution is the coefficient-level operation; PGF multiplication is the transform-level operation.\" → TB-R02 → Gate",
      "content": "{\"id\":\"TA-19\",\"title\":\"PARTIAL (MC-3: PGFs add instead of multiply) → \\\"For INDEPENDENT X,Y: G_{X+Y}(z)=E[z^{X+Y}]=E[z^X·z^Y]=E[z^X]E[z^Y]=G_X(z)G_Y(z). They MULTIPLY. Intuition: the PGF of a sum is the PRODUCT of PGFs (like Laplace transforms of convolutions). PMF convolution is the coefficient-level operation; PGF multiplication is the transform-level operation.\\\" → TB-R02 → Gate\",\"primitives\":[],\"addresses\":[\"MC-3\"]}",
